# Byte-stability policy for this run directory (same rationale as the v5 plan dir).
#
# checkpoint.json records a sha256 for every produced file in this directory. Those
# hashes are computed over the raw working-tree bytes, so the repository must store
# exactly those bytes: with the machine-wide `core.autocrlf=true`, text files would be
# committed as LF and re-checked-out as CRLF, and a reviewer hashing
# `git show HEAD:<path>` would get a different digest than the one recorded here.
#
# `-text` disables EOL conversion, `-filter`/`-working-tree-encoding` guard against
# any smudge/clean filter, so blob bytes == working-tree bytes for every file below.
#
# SCOPE / HISTORY (A-DR2-01): this file first took effect with the commit that added
# it. Four files (command-manifest.json, evidence/cli-help-matrix.json and the two
# catalog-companion-observation files) had already been staged before that commit, so
# their blobs were stored LF. They were renormalised (`git add --renormalize`) in the
# v0.3 correction commit; from that commit on the promise holds for every file here.
# Verify with the produced_files_verification block in checkpoint.json, which compares
# each recorded digest against `git cat-file blob HEAD:<path>`.
* -text -eol -filter -working-tree-encoding

